#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:19
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:25
msgid "serveStatic(root, options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:27
msgid ""
"Create a new middleware function to serve files from within a given root "
"directory. The file to serve will be determined by combining `req.url` "
"with the provided root directory. When a file is not found, instead of "
"sending a 404 response, this module will instead call `next()` to move on"
" to the next middleware, allowing for stacking and fall-backs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:33
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:35
msgid "acceptRanges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:37
msgid ""
"Enable or disable accepting ranged requests, defaults to true. Disabling "
"this will not send `Accept-Ranges` and ignore the contents of the `Range`"
" request header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:41
msgid "cacheControl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:43
msgid ""
"Enable or disable setting `Cache-Control` response header, defaults to "
"true. Disabling this will ignore the `immutable` and `maxAge` options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:46
msgid "dotfiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:48
msgid ""
"Set how \"dotfiles\" are treated when encountered. A dotfile is a file or"
" directory that begins with a dot (\".\"). Note this check is done on the"
" path itself without checking if the path actually exists on the disk. If"
" `root` is specified, only the dotfiles above the root are checked (i.e. "
"the root itself can be within a dotfile when set to \"deny\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:55
msgid "`'allow'` No special treatment for dotfiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:56
msgid "`'deny'` Deny a request for a dotfile and 403/`next()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:57
msgid "`'ignore'` Pretend like the dotfile does not exist and 404/`next()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:59
msgid ""
"The default value is similar to `'ignore'`, with the exception that this "
"default will not ignore the files within a directory that begins with a "
"dot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:62
msgid "etag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:64
msgid "Enable or disable etag generation, defaults to true."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:66
msgid "extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:68
msgid ""
"Set file extension fallbacks. When set, if a file is not found, the given"
" extensions will be added to the file name and search for. The first that"
" exists will be served. Example: `['html', 'htm']`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:72
msgid "The default value is `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:74
msgid "fallthrough"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:76
msgid ""
"Set the middleware to have client errors fall-through as just unhandled "
"requests, otherwise forward a client error. The difference is that client"
" errors like a bad request or a request to a non-existent file will cause"
" this middleware to simply `next()` to your next middleware when this "
"value is `true`. When this value is `false`, these errors (even 404s), "
"will invoke `next(err)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:83
msgid ""
"Typically `true` is desired such that multiple physical directories can "
"be mapped to the same web address or for routes to fill in non-existent "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:86
msgid ""
"The value `false` can be used if this middleware is mounted at a path "
"that is designed to be strictly a single file system directory, which "
"allows for short-circuiting 404s for less overhead. This middleware will "
"also reply to all methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:91
msgid "The default value is `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:93
msgid "immutable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:95
msgid ""
"Enable or disable the `immutable` directive in the `Cache-Control` "
"response header, defaults to `false`. If set to `true`, the `maxAge` "
"option should also be specified to enable caching. The `immutable` "
"directive will prevent supported clients from making conditional requests"
" during the life of the `maxAge` option to check if the file has changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:101
msgid "index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:103
msgid ""
"By default this module will send \"index.html\" files in response to a "
"request on a directory. To disable this set `false` or to supply a new "
"index pass a string or an array in preferred order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:107
msgid "lastModified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:109
msgid ""
"Enable or disable `Last-Modified` header, defaults to true. Uses the file"
" system's last modified value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:112
msgid "maxAge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:114
msgid ""
"Provide a max-age in milliseconds for http caching, defaults to 0. This "
"can also be a string accepted by the "
"[ms](https://www.npmjs.org/package/ms#readme) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:118
msgid "redirect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:120
msgid "Redirect to trailing \"/\" when the pathname is a dir. Defaults to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:122
msgid "setHeaders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:124
msgid ""
"Function to set custom headers on response. Alterations to the headers "
"need to occur synchronously. The function is called as `fn(res, path, "
"stat)`, where the arguments are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:128
msgid "`res` the response object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:129
msgid "`path` the file path that is being sent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/serve-static_README.md:130
msgid "`stat` the stat object of the file that is being sent"
msgstr ""

